debian/README.Debian
====================

gofaxserver
-----------

This package installs the gofaxserver binary built from
`gofaxserver/cmd/gofaxserver/main.go` plus a sample configuration file at
`/etc/gofaxserver/config.json.sample`.

Post-install steps
------------------

1. Create the database and user (see README.md "Database Setup").

2. Create a dedicated system user (the package does this automatically):

       adduser --system --group --no-create-home --home /var/lib/gofaxserver gofax

3. Copy and edit the configuration:

       sudo cp /etc/gofaxserver/config.json.sample /etc/gofaxserver/config.json
       sudo chmod 600 /etc/gofaxserver/config.json
       sudoedit /etc/gofaxserver/config.json
       # - set web.api_key to a strong random value
       # - set psk to a strong random value (used to encrypt tenant-user passwords)
       # - configure the database.* and freeswitch.* sections

4. Install and configure FreeSWITCH separately (use the `examples/freeswitch/`
   tree from the source repo as a starting point for `autoload_configs/` and
   `gateways/`).

5. Enable and start the service:

       sudo systemctl daemon-reload
       sudo systemctl enable --now gofaxserver

6. Verify the API is up:

       curl -u admin:YOUR_API_KEY http://localhost:8080/admin/faxes
